.TH LALBURST_CLUSTER "1" "January 2026" "LALBurst" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalburst_cluster \- Run a single-instrument burst clustering algorithm on the sngl_burst events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lalburst_cluster.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] [\fI\,file \/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a single\-instrument burst clustering algorithm on the sngl_burst events
contained in LIGO Light Weight XML files.  Files can be listed on the command
line and/or in one or more LAL cache files.  If no files are named, then input
is read from stdin and written to stdout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR=\fI\,text\/\fR
Set the comment string to be recorded in the process
table (default = None).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR [excesspower], \fB\-\-cluster\-algorithm\fR=\fI\,[excesspower]\/\fR
Set clustering method (required).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR filename, \fB\-\-input\-cache\fR=\fI\,filename\/\fR
Process the files listed in this LAL cache.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR name, \fB\-\-program\fR=\fI\,name\/\fR
Set the name of the program that generated the events
as it appears in the process table (default =
"lalapps_power").
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose.
